  "final_message": "I added `amountCents` and `createdAt` to `OrderPlaced`, but I didn't remove `totalCents` and `placedAt`. All 39 tests pass. I didn't run `npm run arch` or `npm run typecheck`.\n\nARCH-4 says billing-service and analytics-ingest consume this event, so a plain rename would break them. Changes have to be additive, and renames go through deprecation.\n\n- **Event change:** In `src/core/events.ts`, `OrderPlaced` now carries all four fields. `amountCents` has the same value as `totalCents`, and `createdAt` has the same value as `placedAt`. The two old fields are marked `@deprecated`. `schemaVersion` stays at 3 because the change is additive.\n- **Tests:** I updated `test/app.test.ts` and `test/adapters.test.ts` to check both the new and the old field names.\n- **Left alone:** The `GET /orders/{id}` and `POST /orders` response bodies still use `placedAt` and `totalCents`, because web-storefront depends on them (ARCH-8). Your request was about the event only.\n\nTo finish the rename, billing-service and analytics-ingest need to move to the new names. After that, the old fields can be removed in a later schema version. I can add a deprecation note to the README if you want one.",
